00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:42,600
Even though the coverage
goes up, the pass at one--

259
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,600
or basically, how
we can generate,

260
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:47,280
select the correct response--

261
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:53,060
fails around 50 or less for
the majority voting approach.

262
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:56,080
But here, they're showing
that, up until 400,

263
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:59,600
they can increase the accuracy,
and the verifier is still

264
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,260
useful.

265
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:10,960
Yes, but when they
have-- so they

266
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:13,700
do have the true
labels per problem.

267
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,900
And then, when they are
testing this verifier,

268
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:19,040
the verifier ranks
these at each point.

269
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:22,520
Say, for 400, these
400 solutions,

270
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:25,920
they take the highest
score, and they

271
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:27,392
compare that against
ground truth,

272
00:16:27,392 --> 00:16:29,600
and that's what they're
