of how it generalizes,

532
00:31:24,520 --> 00:31:31,120
but PRM is better than
majority voting overall,

533
00:31:31,120 --> 00:31:34,320
and it can tolerate a
whole lot more distribution

534
00:31:34,320 --> 00:31:37,680
shift than majority voting.

535
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:43,480
And so, overall, this seems like
a much better approach here.

536
00:31:43,480 --> 00:31:46,120
Any questions?

537
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,440
Yes?

538
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:51,640
So PRMs obviously could lead
to false credit assignment

539
00:31:51,640 --> 00:31:53,880
