00:33:18,960 --> 00:33:21,620
But they did try to manage
that, and I believe some

568
00:33:21,620 --> 00:33:23,320
of the graphs-- they do that.

569
00:33:23,320 --> 00:33:25,220
But that's a good point.

570
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:25,780
Yes?

571
00:33:25,780 --> 00:33:29,020
What does "majority voting"
mean in this context?

572
00:33:29,020 --> 00:33:33,860
So "majority voting"
is you have n samples.

573
00:33:33,860 --> 00:33:38,520
You don't have any access
to any reward model.

574
00:33:38,520 --> 00:33:42,020
You just see which sample or
solution is repeated most,

575
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:44,200
and you take that as
your final answer.

576
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:46,580
[INAUDIBLE] the
reasoning process,

577
00:33:46,580 --> 00:33:49,320
so are you also going to match
on the reasoning process?

578
00:33:49,320 --> 00:33:54,140
No, you look into the
final answer in this case.

579
00:33:54,140 --> 00:33:58,580
In this case, are they using
the same PRM at 100k for all

580
00:33:58,580 --> 00:33:59,520
of those tasks?

581
00:33:59,520 --> 00:34:03,650
Or are they using different
terms for each [INAUDIBLE]?

582
00:34:03,650 --> 00:34:05,790
Because they're talking
