00:35:04,920 --> 00:35:08,480
The reasoning step would
just be numerator x,

605
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:10,800
and then x equals to 14.

606
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:13,880
And how does the PRM avoid
that kind of real [? typing ?]

607
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:14,940
scenario?

608
00:35:14,940 --> 00:35:17,840
I think the model
directly skips some steps

609
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:22,280
and directly generates the
answer, like, [? speeds ?]

610
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,960
some of the processes.

611
00:35:23,960 --> 00:35:26,280
So these programs
are trained like--

612
00:35:26,280 --> 00:35:29,120
programs can also see
the previous steps,

613
00:35:29,120 --> 00:35:30,880
like the question's
previous step.

614
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:32,400
Here is the current step.

615
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:33,880
Score it.

616
00:35:33,880 --> 00:35:35,200
Right?

617
00:35:35,200 --> 00:35:37,580
So if x is 14, then
